   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A shop sets the price of an item at \\( p(t) \\) dollars and sells \\( n(t) \\) items per day, where \\( t \\) is measured in weeks. At \\( t = 5 \\), \\( p(5) = 9 \\), \\( p'(5) = 2 \\), \\( n(5) = 12 \\), and \\( n'(5) = 2 \\). The daily revenue is \\( R(t) = p(t)n(t) \\) dollars per day. Find the value of \\( R'(5) \\), in dollars per day per week."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 42
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( t = 5 \\): \\( p(5) = 9 \\), \\( p'(5) = 2 \\), \\( n(5) = 12 \\), \\( n'(5) = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( (pn)'(5) = p'(5)n(5) + p(5)n'(5) \\).",
         "mathjson": 9
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( (2)(12) + (9)(2) = 42 \\).",
         "mathjson": 42
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( R'(5) = 42 \\): revenue is changing at 42 dollars per day per week at \\( t = 5 \\).",
         "mathjson": 42
      }
   ],
